// ADR 0025 S0 (§7 rung 1) — MUTATING THE CONTAINER WHILE A LEAF BATCH LIVES.
//
// The batch is a VIEW into the leaf's own PdtBuf slots — zero copy — and
// `insert` `tree_release`s the tree the leaf hangs off, so an admitted program
// here reads freed memory. Rung 1 says this is a BORROW-CHECK error and never
// a counter: the batch is `#[borrow_carrying]`-tied to the stream, the stream
// to `&C`, and the mutators take `&mut self`.
//
// THIS IS A DIFFERENT SURFACE FROM fail/ctr_family_mut_while_cursor, which the
// req.1 prerequisite landed: that one holds the per-row CURSOR, this one holds
// the BATCH — a type that did not exist then, reached through the split pull
// (`advance()` + `batch(&c)`) that S0's producer emits.
//
// ⚠ AND IT IS THE SPLIT PULL ON PURPOSE — BUT NO LONGER FOR THE ORIGINAL
// REASON. As first written, this header said the `Option<B>` form of §1
// (`next_batch()` / `BatchStream::next`) did NOT refuse the same program:
// `Option::Some(b)` takes the batch BY VALUE, provenance did not survive a
// by-value generic constructor, so the borrow was laundered and the mutation
// was admitted. THAT WAS COMPILER DEFECT D1, and it is CLOSED (re-measured
// 2026-08-11, same day): a loan now follows the holder graph, `next_batch()`
// is sound, and the hole this paragraph used to declare IS NOW PINNED — as
// fail/ctr_family_mut_while_next_batch (the D1 repro verbatim) with its admit
// twin pass/ctr_family_next_batch_then_mut.
//
// SO THIS FIXTURE IS NOT THE ONLY SOUND DOOR ANYMORE, AND IT STILL STAYS. The
// two doors launder differently — this one through a `&self` method plus a
// witness argument, the other through `Option` composition and `unwrap` — and
// a checker can lose one without the other. Two surfaces, two pairs.
//
// The admit twin is pass/ctr_family_batch_then_mut: the refusal message here
// is byte-identical to what an over-refusing checker prints, so neither half
// stands alone.
//
// AND THE REFUSAL IS THE BATCH'S, not the stream's — measured by deleting the
// `s.batch(&c)` line from THIS program: it then COMPILES, because the stream's
// borrow ends at its last use (`advance()` above the insert). Hold the stream
// live ACROSS the mutation instead (advance again below it) and the same
// diagnostic returns, so both borrows are real; this fixture is the one that
// pins the BATCH's.
package ctr_family_mut_while_batch;

use logos.lcm.canon.container_item;
use logos.lcm.canon.metaclass;
use logos.mem.bt.map;
use logos.mem.bt.memstore;
use logos.mem.sync;
use logos.lang.stream;

pub container Led {
    kind ordered_map;
    entry { key: u64, val: u64 }
    measure count;
    measure max(key);
}

fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut store: Arc<MemoryStore> = store_new();
    let snap: Arc<dyn Snapshot> = store_fork_arc(&mut store);
    let mut c = create_ctr::<typeof(Led)>(&snap, 1u64);
    c.insert(1u64, 10u64);
    let mut s = c.leaf_batches();
    let ok: bool = s.advance();
    let b = s.batch(&c);              // the batch borrows the leaf…
    c.insert(3u64, 30u64);            // …so THIS must be refused
    return if ok { b.len() as i32 } else { 9i32 };
}
